      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T02:54:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we will need to update this. this is technically a breaking change, but this config was never officially defined.\n\nBased on the latest discussions, we will need a couple of new definitions. We have not prototyped vendor-defined enums, so this may be tricky. Maybe\n\nstruct C2SystemResource {\n  uint32_t id;  // this is a uint32_t based enum, where the platform will define some values, and reserve a range for vendor values\n  resource_kind_t kind;\n  uint64_t amount;\n}\n\n(vendors will need to shadow this with their own identical vendor-struct and their vendor-enum, so that the parameterDescriptor will pick of the named values.)\n\nThe names of the resources will come from the parameterDescriptor for that field.\n\nresource_kind_t can be:\n{ CONST, PER_FRAME, PER_INPUT_BLOCK, PER_OUTPUT_BLOCK } with more to be defined later.\n\nThen the codec-required, system available resources would use C2SystemResource array instead uint64_t[].\n\nAlso we need to mark all of these as \"[PROPOSED]\" to mark that this is still under discussion.\n\nFor global resources, it would make sense to define \"CAPACITY\" and \"EXCLUDED\" (vs. available.)  Excluded means that total capacity is reduced.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1288,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 1288,
        "endChar": 45
